llvm-openmp provides libomp.dll and its import library lib/libomp.lib (no CMake package).

To use it with code compiled with MSVC's /openmp:llvm instead of the toolset's libomp140.x86_64.dll,
link lib/libomp.lib explicitly and drop the default library requested by the compiler:

    set(OpenMP_RUNTIME_MSVC "llvm")
    find_package(OpenMP REQUIRED)
    find_library(LLVM_OPENMP_LIBRARY NAMES libomp REQUIRED NO_SYSTEM_ENVIRONMENT_PATH NO_CMAKE_SYSTEM_PATH)
    target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE OpenMP::OpenMP_CXX "${LLVM_OPENMP_LIBRARY}")
    target_link_options(main PRIVATE "LINKER:/NODEFAULTLIB:libomp.lib" "LINKER:/NODEFAULTLIB:libompd.lib")

The LLVM headers are in include/llvm-openmp (not needed with /openmp:llvm, which uses the toolset's omp.h).
